window.docContents[27].resolve({"/Representation-Formulas___-Variational-Principles___-and-Fixed-Points/Hilbert___s-Problems/#PDEAtlas--Representation-Formulas___-Variational-Principles___-and-Fixed-Points--Hilbert___s-Problems--Hilbert___s-Problems":{"contents":"\n\nThree problems of the list that Hilbert presented in Paris in 1900\n concern the calculus of variations: the 19th, the 20th and the\n23rd. The folder PDE/HilbertProblems is for them. A file there quotes the problem as Hilbert\nasked it and proves an answer for a stated class from the general theory, which stays under its\nown subject. The\nfolder holds the 19th problem for one unknown and uniformly regular integrands, the 20th\nproblem for convex integrands of growth , and the 23rd problem for the simple integral\nand, for a field given by a family of extremals, for the multiple integral.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"PDEAtlas\u0009Representation Formulas, Variational Principles, and Fixed Points\u0009Hilbert's Problems","header":"9.4.1. Hilbert's Problems","id":"/Representation-Formulas___-Variational-Principles___-and-Fixed-Points/Hilbert___s-Problems/#PDEAtlas--Representation-Formulas___-Variational-Principles___-and-Fixed-Points--Hilbert___s-Problems--Hilbert___s-Problems"}});